From bob@example.com Wed Feb 25 11:20:00 2026
From: Bob Martinez <bob@example.com>
To: alice@example.com
Subject: Quick question about blob GC
Message-ID: <msg009@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Feb 2026 11:20:00 +0000
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Alice,

The blob GC grace period is set to 1 hour. Is that enough for a
large cluster where replication might be slow? I'm thinking about
the case where:

1. User uploads attachment
2. Blob is written to node A
3. Before replication to node B, node A runs GC
4. Blob has zero Pebble references on node A (not yet replicated)
5. GC deletes the blob

Should we bump the grace period to 4 hours, or add a "pending
replication" flag?

- Bob

