Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

SECURITY ADVISORY
=================

CVE-2026-1234: IMAP IDLE command denial of service
Severity: Medium (CVSS 5.3)
Affected versions: Bongo 0.8.0 through 0.8.5
Fixed in: Bongo 0.8.6, 0.9.0

Description:
A malformed IDLE continuation could cause the IMAP server to consume
excessive memory by not enforcing a timeout on idle connections.

Mitigation:
Update to Bongo 0.8.6 or later. If unable to update immediately,
set imap.idle_timeout = "5m" in your configuration.

Timeline:
- Feb 10: Reported by security researcher
- Feb 12: Fix developed and tested
- Feb 14: Patch released in 0.8.6
- Feb 19: Public disclosure

Thank you to Dara Okonkwo for responsible disclosure.

--boundary011
Content-Type: text/html; charset="UTF-8"

